<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n13042" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπόλειψις</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εως</span>,
			ἡ, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπολείπω</span>)
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>abandonment,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡ ἀ. τοῦ στρατοπέδου</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Th.
					7.75
				</span></i>
			; <i>defection,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Id.
				4.126
			</span></i>; <i>desertion</i> of a husband by his wife (cf. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπολείπω</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					11.1
				</span></i>
			), <i><span class="en">
				D.
				30.15
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπόλειψιν ἀπογράφεσθαι</span>
			(v. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπογράφω</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					111.2
				</span></i>
			) ib.<i><span class="en">
				17
			</span></i> (but also, 
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπόπεμψις, ἀ.
				γράψασθαι</span>
			
			<i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				2.100e
			</span></i>); <i>desertion</i> by soldiers, seamen, etc., <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>HG</u>
				4.1.28
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				D.
				50.11
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> intr.,
				<i>deficiency,</i> of rivers, <i>failing,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Mete.</u>
				351a21
			</span></i> (pl.); of the moon, <i>waning,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>GA</u>
				767a5
			</span></i>; of the sun, <i>departure to southern hemisphere,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Jul.
				<u>Or.</u>
				4.137d
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>death,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δοιὴ δὲ θνητῶν γένεσις, δοιὴ δ᾽ ἀ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Emp.
					17.3
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. τοῦ ζην</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hyp.
					<u>Epit.</u>
					24
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐκ τοῦ ὄντος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Porph.
					<u>Sent.</u>
					20
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b> in Law,
				<i>default,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Cod.Just.
				1.4.18
			</span></i>.</div>
